+//The S-CPU's cooperative thread, as the other chips resume it
+//(scheduler.resume(cpu.thread)). The harness runs a routine's C on a thread
+//of its own and makes that thread the S-CPU's while the C runs, so a chip
+//the C's bus accesses synchronize with comes back to the C; it puts the
+//S-CPU's own thread back when the C stops for its task's next turn.
+extern "C" void** snesbox_cpu_thread() {
+  return (void**)&SuperFamicom::cpu.thread;
+}
